      "extract": "For $g=su(N)$, the centre of the group is $Z(SU(N)) = {\\bf Z}_N$. When the gauge group is $G=S(N)$, all electric line operators are allowed; that is $z^e=0,1,2,\\ldots, N-1$. In contrast, the magnetic line operators are restricted to lie on the magnetic root lattice, meaning that $z^m=0$. The resulting set of line operators for $SU(3)$ are shown in Figure \\ref{su3lines}a, plotted in the $(z^e,z^m)$ lattice. The",
